language 0.1.0
module syntax
  means
    The written form of a formal language: the units a text is made of, the
    rules by which their order is admissible, and the tree a text is read
    into, independent of what the text describes.

entity grammar : thing
  means
    grammar: a formal description of the admissible order of the units of a
    language.

entity production : thing
  means
    production: a rule of a grammar defining one construct through other
    constructs and units.

entity terminal : thing
  means
    terminal: a unit of a grammar not defined through others and standing in
    a text as it is written.

entity nonterminal : thing
  means
    nonterminal: a unit of a grammar defined by productions and never
    standing in a text by itself.

entity token : thing
  means
    token: an indivisible unit of a text, singled out by its spelling and
    carrying the kind it was recognised as.

entity token-class : thing
  means
    token class: a named set of spellings recognised as tokens of one kind.

entity keyword : thing
  means
    keyword: a word reserved by a language and recognised by its spelling
    alone.

entity literal : thing
  means
    literal: a token whose value is its own spelling, taken without further
    interpretation.

entity comment : thing
  means
    comment: a part of a text carried through parsing without effect on the
    constructs it stands among.

entity escape-sequence : thing
  means
    escape sequence: a spelling by which a character otherwise significant
    to the grammar is written as itself.

entity indentation : thing
  means
    indentation: the leading blank part of a line, by whose width the
    nesting of constructs is judged.

entity block : thing
  means
    block: a run of lines belonging to the construct that opens them.

entity syntax-tree : thing
  means
    syntax tree: the constructs of one text arranged as the grammar admits
    them, one node per construct.

entity syntax-node : thing
  means
    syntax node: a single construct of a syntax tree, together with its
    place in the text it was read from.

entity lookahead : thing
  means
    lookahead: the number of units a parser may examine ahead of the one it
    is deciding on.
